re", "Terrible Power", "Telepathy", "Resonance Void", "Dark Majesty", "Sinister Guile", "Feral Whispers", "Versatile"], "quiet": 3, "loud": 6, "wallet": 4, "bank": 40, "playbookXp": 10, "attributeXp": 8, "builtInArmor": false, "actionMax": 5, "harmSlots": {"passing": 2, "major": 2, "critical": 1, "mortal": 1}, "source": "Blades ’68 playbooks v6 page 10; book v1.0.1 pp.334–340", "creation": "Hunt, Prowl, Skirmish, Attune, Command and Sway start at 1. On transformation add previous ratings, maximum 4. Choose four Deadlocks and two Dark Servants; retain only Echo special abilities. Begin with Dayfire and one more trait.", "xpTrigger": "dominance or slaying without mercy", "abilityGuidance": "Dark Majesty selects one attribute: only its actions can reach 5; its +1 resistance bonus is separate from action dots. Each new non-Versatile vampiric trait adds a stricture. Sinister Guile is a deliberate downtime choice. Terrible Power costs 1 Stress for superhuman speed/strength; Telepathy costs 1 for extraordinary senses. Resonance Void conceals you from entities, with 2 Stress to avert living observers. Feral Whispers uses Attune with animals. All costs and fictional outcomes are deliberate.", "conditionKind": "vampire", "fixedAbilities": ["Vampire"], "abilityChoiceGuidance": "Vampire is preselected. Choose one more trait at creation.", "resourceGuidance": "Stress 12; all four Deadlocks start filled. Mortal Harm or another Deadlock overwhelms you: record Critical Incapacitated until feeding. Paranormal Harm then destroys you. Feeding is one Hunt downtime activity: clear highest die Stress and mark 4 healing ticks; feeding is the only healing method."}'::jsonb);
